    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to Pre-Historic India.",
    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Does &quot;Pre-Historic&quot; Mean?</h3>\n<p>The word &quot;Pre-Historic&quot; is made of two parts. Pre = Before. Historic = History (written records). So, Pre-Historic means the time before humans learned to write.</p>\n<p>Why is this important? Because there is no written proof. We only know about this time from things they left behind — stone tools, bones, cave paintings, and pottery. Archaeologists dig the ground and find these things.</p>\n<p>When was this time? From about 5,00,000 BC to 1,000 BC.</p>\n<h3>Part 2: The Four Phases of Pre-Historic India</h3>\n<p>Palaeolithic Age | 5,00,000 BC - 10,000 BC | Old Stone Age</p>\n<p>Mesolithic Age | 10,000 BC - 6,000 BC | Middle Stone Age</p>\n<p>Neolithic Age | 6,000 BC - 1,000 BC | New Stone Age</p>\n<p>Chalcolithic Age | 3,000 BC - 500 BC | Copper-Stone Age</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Palaeolithic Age (Old Stone Age)</h3>\n<p>Time Period: 5,00,000 BC - 10,000 BC</p>\n<p>Palaeo = Old. Lithic = Stone. Palaeolithic means Old Stone Age.</p>\n<p>Tools: Hand Axe, Cleaver, Chopper. Material: quartzite, flint, limestone.</p>\n<p>Occupation: Hunting, gathering, fishing. Society: Small nomadic groups. Shelter: Caves, rock shelters. Fire: Discovered in this period. Food: Raw meat, fruits, nuts, roots. Burial: No evidence of burial. Art: No art.</p>\n<p>Important sites: Bhimbetka (Madhya Pradesh) - Famous for rock paintings. Soan Valley (Punjab, Pakistan) - Stone tools found. Narmada Valley (Madhya Pradesh) - Hand axes found.</p>\n<p>Sub-Phases: Lower Palaeolithic (5,00,000 BC - 50,000 BC) - Hand axes, cleavers. Middle Palaeolithic (50,000 BC - 40,000 BC) - Smaller tools, scrapers. Upper Palaeolithic (40,000 BC - 10,000 BC) - Blade tools, burins.</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Mesolithic Age (Middle Stone Age)</h3>\n<p>Time Period: 10,000 BC - 6,000 BC. Meso = Middle. Lithic = Stone.</p>\n<p>Tools: Microliths (small stone tools).</p>\n<p>Occupation: Hunting, gathering, fishing. Society: Small nomadic groups. Shelter: Caves, rock shelters. Domestication: Started taming animals (dog, sheep, goat). Burial: Evidence of burial. Art: Rock paintings (Bhimbetka).</p>\n<p>Important sites: Bhimbetka (MP) - Rock paintings. Langhnaj (Gujarat) - Microliths. Bagor (Rajasthan) - Microliths. Sarai Nahar Rai (UP) - Burial.</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Neolithic Age (New Stone Age)</h3>\n<p>Time Period: 6,000 BC - 1,000 BC. Neo = New. Lithic = Stone.</p>\n<p>Tools: Polished Stone Tools, Celts, Adzes.</p>\n<p>Occupation: Agriculture, animal domestication. Society: Settled villages. Shelter: Mud houses, pit houses. Crops: Wheat, barley, rice. Pottery: Yes. Burial: Evidence of burial.</p>\n<p>Important sites: Mehrgarh (Balochistan) - Earliest evidence of agriculture. Burzahom (Kashmir) - Pit houses. Chirand (Bihar) - Pottery. Koldihwa (UP) - Rice husk.</p>\n<h3>Part 6: Chalcolithic Age (Copper-Stone Age)</h3>\n<p>Time Period: 3,000 BC - 500 BC. Chalco = Copper. Lithic = Stone.</p>\n<p>Tools: Copper Tools, Stone Tools.</p>\n<p>Occupation: Agriculture. Society: Settled villages. Pottery: Yes. Burial: Evidence of burial.</p>\n<p>Important sites: Inamgaon (Maharashtra) - Agriculture. Navdatoli (MP) - Pottery. Ahar (Rajasthan) - Copper tools.</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Important Pre-Historic Sites</h3>\n<p>Bhimbetka, Madhya Pradesh, Palaeolithic to Mesolithic, Rock paintings</p>\n<p>Soan Valley, Punjab (Pakistan), Palaeolithic, Stone tools</p>\n<p>Narmada Valley, Madhya Pradesh, Palaeolithic, Hand axes</p>\n<p>Langhnaj, Gujarat, Mesolithic, Microliths</p>\n<p>Bagor, Rajasthan, Mesolithic, Microliths</p>\n<p>Sarai Nahar Rai, Uttar Pradesh, Mesolithic, Burial</p>\n<p>Mehrgarh, Balochistan, Neolithic, Agriculture</p>\n<p>Burzahom, Jammu &amp; Kashmir, Neolithic, Pit houses</p>\n<p>Chirand, Bihar, Neolithic, Pottery</p>\n<p>Koldihwa, Uttar Pradesh, Neolithic, Rice husk</p>\n<p>Inamgaon, Maharashtra, Chalcolithic, Agriculture</p>\n<p>Navdatoli, Madhya Pradesh, Chalcolithic, Pottery</p>\n<p>Ahar, Rajasthan, Chalcolithic, Copper tools</p>\n<h3>Part 8: Important Facts for SSC</h3>\n<p>Old Stone Age | Palaeolithic Age</p>\n<p>Middle Stone Age | Mesolithic Age</p>\n<p>New Stone Age | Neolithic Age</p>\n<p>Copper-Stone Age | Chalcolithic Age</p>\n<p>Famous for Rock Paintings | Bhimbetka (MP)</p>\n<p>Earliest Evidence of Agriculture | Mehrgarh</p>\n<p>Famous for Pit Houses | Burzahom (J&amp;K)</p>\n<p>Earliest Evidence of Rice | Koldihwa (UP)</p>\n<p>Famous for Chalcolithic Culture | Inamgaon</p>\n<p>Discovery of Fire | Palaeolithic Age</p>\n<p>Start of Agriculture | Neolithic Age</p>\n<p>First Use of Metal | Chalcolithic Age</p>\n<p>Microliths | Mesolithic Age</p>\n<p>Polished Tools | Neolithic Age</p>\n<p><b>Q1: Which is the oldest phase of Pre-Historic India? Answer: Palaeolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2: In which period did agriculture start? Answer: Neolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3: Which site is famous for rock paintings? Answer: Bhimbetka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4: Which site is the earliest evidence of agriculture in India? Answer: Mehrgarh</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5: Which site is famous for pit houses? Answer: Burzahom</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6: In which period was fire discovered? Answer: Palaeolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7: Which age is called the Copper-Stone Age? Answer: Chalcolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8: Which age is called the Middle Stone Age? Answer: Mesolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9: Which age is called the New Stone Age? Answer: Neolithic Age</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10: Which age is called the Old Stone Age? Answer: Palaeolithic Age</b></p>"
