    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Was the Indus Valley Civilization?</h3>\n<p>The Indus Valley Civilization (IVC) is also called the Harappan Civilization because Harappa was the first city discovered.</p>\n<p>Duration: About 3300 BC to 1300 BC. Mature Period: 2600 BC to 1900 BC.</p>\n<p>Location: Mostly in Pakistan and North-West India (Punjab, Haryana, Rajasthan, Gujarat, Uttar Pradesh).</p>\n<p>Discovery: 1826 - Charles Masson first mentioned Harappa. 1921 - Harappa was excavated by Daya Ram Sahni. 1922 - Mohenjo-Daro was excavated by R.D. Banerjee.</p>\n<h3>Part 2: Discovery of Major Sites</h3>\n<p>1826 | Harappa (First Mention) | Charles Masson</p>\n<p>1921 | Harappa (Excavated) | Daya Ram Sahni</p>\n<p>1922 | Mohenjo-Daro | R.D. Banerjee</p>\n<p>1927 | Sutkagendor | Aurel Stein</p>\n<p>1931 | Lothal | S.R. Rao</p>\n<p>1935 | Chanhudaro | N.G. Majumdar</p>\n<p>1953 | Kalibangan | A. Ghosh</p>\n<p>1955 | Dholavira | J.P. Joshi</p>\n<p>1958 | Banawali | R.S. Bisht</p>\n<p>1964 | Surkotada | J.P. Joshi</p>\n<p>1974 | Rakhigarhi | Vasant Shinde</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Extent of IVC</h3>\n<p>North | Manda | Jammu &amp; Kashmir | Chenab</p>\n<p>South | Daimabad | Maharashtra | Pravara</p>\n<p>East | Alamgirpur | Western Uttar Pradesh | Hindon</p>\n<p>West | Sutkagendor | Balochistan (Pakistan) | Dasht</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Major Cities</h3>\n<p>Harappa: River Ravi. Granaries, Cemetery R-37. Punjab (Pakistan).</p>\n<p>Mohenjo-Daro: River Indus. Great Bath, Bronze Dancing Girl, Pashupati Seal. Sindh (Pakistan).</p>\n<p>Lothal: River Bhogava. Dockyard, Rice husk. Gujarat (India).</p>\n<p>Kalibangan: River Ghaggar. Ploughed field, Fire altars. Rajasthan (India).</p>\n<p>Dholavira: River Luni. Water reservoir, Signboard. Gujarat (India).</p>\n<p>Rakhigarhi: River Ghaggar. Largest IVC site in India. Haryana (India).</p>\n<p>Chanhudaro: River Indus. Bead making factory. Sindh (Pakistan).</p>\n<p>Surkotada: Horse bones. Gujarat (India).</p>\n<p>Banawali: River Ghaggar. Terracotta plough figure. Haryana (India).</p>\n<p>Sutkagendor: River Dasht. Westernmost site. Balochistan (Pakistan).</p>\n<p>Manda: River Chenab. Northernmost site. Jammu &amp; Kashmir (India).</p>\n<p>Daimabad: River Pravara. Southernmost site. Maharashtra (India).</p>\n<p>Alamgirpur: River Hindon. Easternmost site. Uttar Pradesh (India).</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Town Planning</h3>\n<p>Grid Pattern: Roads cut at 90 degrees.</p>\n<p>Two Parts: Citadel (Upper Town) and Lower Town.</p>\n<p>Drainage System: Covered drains, manholes.</p>\n<p>Great Bath: Found at Mohenjo-Daro.</p>\n<p>Granaries: Found at Harappa and Mohenjo-Daro.</p>\n<p>Houses: Made of baked bricks.</p>\n<p>Brick Size: Standard ratio 1:2:4.</p>\n<p>Main Street: 10.5 meters wide at Mohenjo-Daro.</p>\n<h3>Part 6: Economy</h3>\n<p>Agriculture: Wheat, barley, rice, peas, cotton.</p>\n<p>Ploughed Field: Found at Kalibangan.</p>\n<p>Trade: Internal and External.</p>\n<p>External Trade: Mesopotamia, Egypt, Persia.</p>\n<p>Main Port: Lothal.</p>\n<p>Seals: Made of steatite.</p>\n<p>Famous Seal: Pashupati Seal.</p>\n<p>Metals Used: Copper, bronze, gold, silver.</p>\n<p>No Iron: Iron was NOT known.</p>\n<p>Bead Making: Center at Chanhudaro.</p>\n<p>Cotton: First civilization to produce cotton.</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Religion</h3>\n<p>Mother Goddess: Worshipped for fertility.</p>\n<p>Pashupati: Three-faced male deity (proto-Shiva).</p>\n<p>Nature Worship: Trees (Pipal), Animals (Bull, Unicorn).</p>\n<p>Temples: No evidence.</p>\n<p>Fire Altars: Found at Kalibangan and Lothal.</p>\n<p>Unicorn: Most common animal on seals.</p>\n<h3>Part 8: Society</h3>\n<p>Matriarchal: Mother Goddess worshipped.</p>\n<p>Caste System: No evidence.</p>\n<p>Dress: Men - Dhoti and Shawl. Women - Skirts and Ornaments.</p>\n<p>Ornaments: Gold, silver, copper.</p>\n<p>Food: Wheat, barley, milk, dates, fruits, fish.</p>\n<p>Games: Dice games.</p>\n<p>No Weapons: Very few weapons found.</p>\n<h3>Part 9: Art and Craft</h3>\n<p>Bronze Dancing Girl: Found at Mohenjo-Daro.</p>\n<p>Bearded Man: Steatite statue at Mohenjo-Daro.</p>\n<p>Bead Making: Center at Chanhudaro.</p>\n<p>Pottery: Red and black pottery.</p>\n<p>Seals: Steatite, terracotta, copper.</p>\n<p>Bronze Casting: Lost wax technique.</p>\n<h3>Part 10: Script</h3>\n<p>Status: Undeciphered.</p>\n<p>Direction: Right to Left.</p>\n<p>Nature: Pictographic.</p>\n<p>Number of Signs: About 400-600.</p>\n<p>Longest Inscription: 17 signs.</p>\n<h3>Part 11: Decline of IVC</h3>\n<p>Aryan Invasion | Mortimer Wheeler</p>\n<p>Floods | Ernest Mackay</p>\n<p>Climate Change | Gurdip Singh</p>\n<p>Tectonic Movements | M.R. Sahni</p>\n<p>Epidemic | K.U.R. Kennedy</p>\n<p>Drying of Rivers | D.P. Agrawal</p>\n<p>Decline Period: Around 1900 BC.</p>\n<h3>Part 12: Important Facts for SSC</h3>\n<p>Largest IVC Site in India | Rakhigarhi (Haryana)</p>\n<p>Largest IVC Site Overall | Mohenjo-Daro (Pakistan)</p>\n<p>Main Port | Lothal (Gujarat)</p>\n<p>Great Bath | Mohenjo-Daro</p>\n<p>Bronze Dancing Girl | Mohenjo-Daro</p>\n<p>Pashupati Seal | Mohenjo-Daro</p>\n<p>Ploughed Field | Kalibangan</p>\n<p>Dockyard | Lothal</p>\n<p>Horse Bones | Surkotada</p>\n<p>Script | Undeciphered, Right to Left</p>\n<p>First Discovered Site | Harappa (1921)</p>\n<p>First Civilization to Produce Cotton | IVC</p>\n<p>Iron | NOT Known to IVC</p>\n<p>Northernmost Site | Manda (J&amp;K)</p>\n<p>Southernmost Site | Daimabad (Maharashtra)</p>\n<p>Easternmost Site | Alamgirpur (UP)</p>\n<p>Westernmost Site | Sutkagendor (Balochistan)</p>\n<p>Bead Making Center | Chanhudaro</p>\n<p>Fire Altars | Kalibangan, Lothal</p>\n<p>No Citadel | Chanhudaro</p>\n<p><b>Q1: Which is the largest IVC site in India? Answer: Rakhigarhi</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2: Where was the Great Bath found? Answer: Mohenjo-Daro</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3: Which IVC site is known for its Dockyard? Answer: Lothal</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4: The Harappan script is: Answer: Undeciphered</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5: Which IVC site is located in Haryana? Answer: Rakhigarhi</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6: Where were horse bones found in IVC? Answer: Surkotada</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7: Which IVC site is known for bead making? Answer: Chanhudaro</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8: Where was the ploughed field found? Answer: Kalibangan</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9: Which is the northernmost site of IVC? Answer: Manda</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10: Which is the southernmost site of IVC? Answer: Daimabad</b></p>"
