    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Was the Vedic Period?</h3>\n<p>After the Indus Valley Civilization declined, a new culture emerged in India. This was the Vedic Period. It is called &quot;Vedic&quot; because the Vedas were composed during this time.</p>\n<p>Duration: 1500 BC - 600 BC.</p>\n<p>Location: Mainly in the Sapta Sindhu region (Land of Seven Rivers) - Punjab, Haryana, Western Uttar Pradesh.</p>\n<p>Two Parts: Early Vedic Period (Rigvedic Period): 1500 BC - 1000 BC. Later Vedic Period: 1000 BC - 600 BC.</p>\n<h3>Part 2: The Four Vedas</h3>\n<p>Rigveda: 1028 hymns. Book of Hymns. Oldest Veda. Hymns to gods (Indra, Agni, Varuna).</p>\n<p>Samaveda: 1875 hymns. Book of Melodies. Origin of Indian music.</p>\n<p>Yajurveda: 1975 hymns. Book of Rituals. Guide for priests performing sacrifices.</p>\n<p>Atharvaveda: 5977 hymns. Book of Spells. Charms and spells for daily life.</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Other Important Vedic Texts</h3>\n<p>Brahmanas: Explanations of rituals.</p>\n<p>Aranyakas: Forest Texts.</p>\n<p>Upanishads: Philosophical Texts.</p>\n<p>Vedangas: Limbs of Vedas - Shiksha, Kalpa, Vyakarana, Nirukta, Chhanda, Jyotisha.</p>\n<p>Upavedas: Subsidiary Vedas - Ayurveda, Dhanurveda, Gandharvaveda, Shilpaveda.</p>\n<p>Puranas: Mythological texts.</p>\n<p>Epics: Ramayana, Mahabharata.</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Early Vedic Period (1500-1000 BC)</h3>\n<p>Society: Tribal.</p>\n<p>Political System: King (Rajan) was elected.</p>\n<p>Economy: Pastoral (cattle rearing).</p>\n<p>Religion: Nature worship (Indra, Agni, Varuna).</p>\n<p>Women: Respectable position.</p>\n<p>Caste System: Flexible.</p>\n<p>Main God: Indra.</p>\n<p>Cow: Most important animal.</p>\n<p>Wars: Fought for cows (Gavishthi).</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Later Vedic Period (1000-600 BC)</h3>\n<p>Society: Varna system became rigid.</p>\n<p>Political System: King became hereditary.</p>\n<p>Economy: Agriculture became primary.</p>\n<p>Religion: Rituals became complex.</p>\n<p>Women: Position declined.</p>\n<p>Caste System: Rigid.</p>\n<p>Main God: Prajapati.</p>\n<p>Iron: Used in this period.</p>\n<p>Ashramas: Four stages of life.</p>\n<h3>Part 6: Vedic Society</h3>\n<p>Varna System: Brahmins (Priests), Kshatriyas (Warriors), Vaishyas (Traders), Shudras (Servants).</p>\n<p>Ashramas: Brahmacharya (Student), Grihastha (Householder), Vanaprastha (Retired), Sannyasa (Renunciate).</p>\n<p>Women: Early Vedic - Respectable. Later Vedic - Position declined.</p>\n<p>Marriage: Monogamy was common. Polygamy was allowed for kings.</p>\n<p>Education: Gurukul system. Oral transmission.</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Vedic Polity</h3>\n<p>King: Rajan.</p>\n<p>Sabha: Council of elders.</p>\n<p>Samiti: General assembly.</p>\n<p>Vidatha: Oldest assembly.</p>\n<p>Purohita: Chief priest.</p>\n<p>Senani: Commander.</p>\n<p>Gramani: Village headman.</p>\n<p>Bali: Voluntary offering.</p>\n<p>Bhaga: Share of produce.</p>\n<h3>Part 8: Vedic Economy</h3>\n<p>Early Vedic: Pastoral.</p>\n<p>Later Vedic: Agriculture.</p>\n<p>Crops: Wheat, barley, rice.</p>\n<p>Animals: Cow, horse, sheep, goat.</p>\n<p>Trade: Barter system.</p>\n<p>Gavishthi: Search for cows.</p>\n<h3>Part 9: Vedic Religion</h3>\n<p>Early Vedic: Nature worship.</p>\n<p>Later Vedic: Rituals became complex.</p>\n<p>Indra: God of rain and war.</p>\n<p>Agni: God of fire.</p>\n<p>Varuna: God of water.</p>\n<p>Prajapati: Creator God.</p>\n<p>Yajna: Sacrifice.</p>\n<p>No Idols: No idol worship.</p>\n<p>No Temples: No temples.</p>\n<h3>Part 10: Important Terms</h3>\n<p>Rajan: King. Sabha: Council of elders. Samiti: General assembly. Vidatha: Oldest assembly. Purohita: Chief priest. Senani: Commander. Gramani: Village headman. Gavishthi: Search for cows. Bali: Voluntary offering. Bhaga: Share of produce. Yajna: Sacrifice. Varna: Caste. Ashrama: Stage of life. Gurukul: School.</p>\n<h3>Part 11: Important Facts for SSC</h3>\n<p>Oldest Veda | Rigveda</p>\n<p>Book of Music | Samaveda</p>\n<p>Book of Rituals | Yajurveda</p>\n<p>Book of Spells | Atharvaveda</p>\n<p>Main God (Early Vedic) | Indra</p>\n<p>Main God (Later Vedic) | Prajapati</p>\n<p>King (Early Vedic) | Elected</p>\n<p>King (Later Vedic) | Hereditary</p>\n<p>Main Occupation (Early Vedic) | Cattle rearing</p>\n<p>Main Occupation (Later Vedic) | Agriculture</p>\n<p>Iron | Used in Later Vedic</p>\n<p>Women (Early Vedic) | Respectable</p>\n<p>Women (Later Vedic) | Declined</p>\n<p>Caste System | Flexible to Rigid</p>\n<p>Sabha | Council of elders</p>\n<p>Samiti | General assembly</p>\n<p>Vidatha | Oldest assembly</p>\n<p>Gavishthi | Search for cows</p>\n<p><b>Q1: Which is the oldest Veda? Answer: Rigveda</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2: Which Veda is the origin of Indian music? Answer: Samaveda</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3: Who was the main god in the Early Vedic Period? Answer: Indra</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4: Who was the main god in the Later Vedic Period? Answer: Prajapati</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5: What was the main occupation in the Early Vedic Period? Answer: Cattle rearing</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6: What was the main occupation in the Later Vedic Period? Answer: Agriculture</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7: What was the king called in the Vedic Period? Answer: Rajan</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8: What was the council of elders called? Answer: Sabha</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9: What was the general assembly called? Answer: Samiti</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10: What was the search for cows called? Answer: Gavishthi</b></p>\n<p><b>Q11: What is the meaning of Bali? Answer: Voluntary offering</b></p>\n<p><b>Q12: What is the meaning of Bhaga? Answer: Share of produce</b></p>\n<p><b>Q13: Which Veda has spells and charms? Answer: Atharvaveda</b></p>\n<p><b>Q14: Which Veda is the book of rituals? Answer: Yajurveda</b></p>\n<p><b>Q15: In which period did the caste system become rigid? Answer: Later Vedic Period</b></p>"
