    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to Mauryan Empire.",
    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Was the Mauryan Empire?</h3>\n<p>The Mauryan Empire was the first pan-Indian empire. It was founded by Chandragupta Maurya in 321 BC.</p>\n<p>Duration: 321 BC - 185 BC.</p>\n<p>Founder: Chandragupta Maurya.</p>\n<p>Greatest Ruler: Ashoka the Great.</p>\n<p>Capital: Pataliputra (modern Patna).</p>\n<p>Last Ruler: Brihadratha (killed by Pushyamitra Shunga in 185 BC).</p>\n<h3>Part 2: Chandragupta Maurya (321 BC - 297 BC)</h3>\n<p>Founder: Chandragupta Maurya.</p>\n<p>Advisor: Chanakya (Kautilya).</p>\n<p>Book: Arthashastra (written by Chanakya).</p>\n<p>Greek Ambassador: Megasthenes.</p>\n<p>Book by Megasthenes: Indica.</p>\n<p>Religion: Jainism (later became a Jain monk).</p>\n<p>Death: 297 BC (Sallekhana - fasting unto death).</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Ashoka the Great (268 BC - 232 BC)</h3>\n<p>Coronation: 268 BC.</p>\n<p>Kalinga War: 261 BC.</p>\n<p>Religion: Buddhism.</p>\n<p>Dhamma: Ashoka's policy of moral law.</p>\n<p>Inscriptions: 33 inscriptions (Rock Edicts, Pillar Edicts).</p>\n<p>Language: Prakrit.</p>\n<p>Script: Brahmi.</p>\n<p>Symbols: Sarnath Lion Capital (National Emblem), Ashoka Chakra (National Flag).</p>\n<p>Stupas: Sanchi Stupa, Sarnath Stupa.</p>\n<p>Death: 232 BC.</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Mauryan Administration</h3>\n<p>Central: King was supreme. Council of Ministers (Mantriparishad).</p>\n<p>Provincial: Empire divided into provinces. Governors (Kumaras) appointed.</p>\n<p>Local: Village headman (Gramani).</p>\n<p>Taxation: Land tax (Bhaga), Trade tax, Irrigation tax.</p>\n<p>Army: Large standing army.</p>\n<p>Spy System: Extensive spy network.</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Mauryan Economy</h3>\n<p>Agriculture: Main occupation. Wheat, barley, rice.</p>\n<p>Trade: Internal and external.</p>\n<p>External Trade: With Rome, Greece, and South-East Asia.</p>\n<p>Currency: Coins (Panas) were used.</p>\n<p>Roads: Built roads for trade and communication.</p>\n<p>Irrigation: Canals and wells were built.</p>\n<h3>Part 6: Ashoka's Dhamma</h3>\n<p>Ahimsa: Non-violence.</p>\n<p>Tolerance: Respect for all religions.</p>\n<p>Obedience to Parents: Respect your father and mother.</p>\n<p>Respect for Teachers: Respect your teachers.</p>\n<p>Kindness to Servants: Be kind to your servants.</p>\n<p>Charity: Give to the poor.</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Ashokan Inscriptions</h3>\n<p>Major Rock Edicts: 14 edicts. Deals with Dhamma.</p>\n<p>Minor Rock Edicts: Personal messages of Ashoka.</p>\n<p>Separate Rock Edicts: Found at Dhauli and Jaugada.</p>\n<p>Major Pillar Edicts: 7 edicts. Deals with Dhamma.</p>\n<p>Minor Pillar Edicts: Deals with Buddhist matters.</p>\n<h3>Part 8: Decline of Mauryan Empire</h3>\n<p>Weak Successors: After Ashoka, the rulers were weak.</p>\n<p>Huna Invasions: Foreign invasions weakened the empire.</p>\n<p>Feudal System: Land grants to officials made them powerful.</p>\n<p>Economic Decline: Heavy taxes and corruption.</p>\n<p>Spread of Buddhism: People became more peace-loving and less warlike.</p>\n<p>In 185 BC, Brihadratha (the last Mauryan ruler) was killed by Pushyamitra Shunga.</p>\n<h3>Part 9: Important Facts for SSC</h3>\n<p>Founder of Mauryan Empire | Chandragupta Maurya</p>\n<p>Advisor of Chandragupta | Chanakya (Kautilya)</p>\n<p>Book by Chanakya | Arthashastra</p>\n<p>Greek Ambassador | Megasthenes</p>\n<p>Book by Megasthenes | Indica</p>\n<p>Greatest Mauryan Ruler | Ashoka</p>\n<p>Kalinga War | 261 BC</p>\n<p>Ashoka's Religion | Buddhism</p>\n<p>Ashoka's Policy | Dhamma</p>\n<p>Ashoka's Inscriptions | 33 inscriptions</p>\n<p>Language of Inscriptions | Prakrit</p>\n<p>Script of Inscriptions | Brahmi</p>\n<p>National Emblem | Sarnath Lion Capital</p>\n<p>National Flag | Ashoka Chakra</p>\n<p>Stupas | Sanchi Stupa, Sarnath Stupa</p>\n<p>Capital of Mauryan Empire | Pataliputra (Patna)</p>\n<p>Last Mauryan Ruler | Brihadratha</p>\n<p>Killed By | Pushyamitra Shunga (185 BC)</p>\n<p><b>Q1: Who founded the Mauryan Empire? Answer: Chandragupta Maurya</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2: Who was the advisor of Chandragupta Maurya? Answer: Chanakya (Kautilya)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3: Which book was written by Chanakya? Answer: Arthashastra</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4: Who was the Greek ambassador in Chandragupta's court? Answer: Megasthenes</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5: Which book was written by Megasthenes? Answer: Indica</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6: Who was the greatest ruler of the Mauryan Empire? Answer: Ashoka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7: Which war did Ashoka fight? Answer: Kalinga War (261 BC)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8: What was Ashoka's policy called? Answer: Dhamma</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9: How many inscriptions did Ashoka leave? Answer: 33</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10: What is the National Emblem of India? Answer: Sarnath Lion Capital</b></p>\n<p><b>Q11: What is on the National Flag of India? Answer: Ashoka Chakra</b></p>\n<p><b>Q12: Where is the Sanchi Stupa located? Answer: Madhya Pradesh</b></p>\n<p><b>Q13: What was the capital of the Mauryan Empire? Answer: Pataliputra (Patna)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q14: Who was the last Mauryan ruler? Answer: Brihadratha</b></p>\n<p><b>Q15: Who killed Brihadratha? Answer: Pushyamitra Shunga</b></p>"
