    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to Post-Mauryan Period.",
    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Was the Post-Mauryan Period?</h3>\n<p>After the Mauryan Empire declined in 185 BC, India was divided into many small kingdoms. This period is called the Post-Mauryan Period. It lasted from 185 BC to 300 AD.</p>\n<p>Main kingdoms: Shunga Dynasty (185 BC - 73 BC), Kushana Dynasty (1st Century AD - 3rd Century AD), Satavahana Dynasty (1st Century BC - 3rd Century AD), Sangam Age (300 BC - 300 AD).</p>\n<h3>Part 2: Shunga Dynasty (185 BC - 73 BC)</h3>\n<p>Founder: Pushyamitra Shunga.</p>\n<p>Capital: Pataliputra.</p>\n<p>Religion: Brahmanism.</p>\n<p>Significance: Patronized Brahmanism. Patanjali wrote Mahabhashya.</p>\n<p>Decline: Overthrown by the Kanvas.</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Kushana Dynasty (1st Century AD - 3rd Century AD)</h3>\n<p>Founder: Kujula Kadphises.</p>\n<p>Greatest Ruler: Kanishka (78 AD - 101 AD).</p>\n<p>Capital: Purushapura (Peshawar).</p>\n<p>Religion: Buddhism.</p>\n<p>Significance: Patronized Buddhism. 4th Buddhist Council at Kundalvana.</p>\n<p>Silk Route: Controlled the Silk Route. Trade with Rome.</p>\n<p>Court Poets: Ashvaghosha (Buddhacharita), Vasumitra.</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Satavahana Dynasty (1st Century BC - 3rd Century AD)</h3>\n<p>Founder: Simuka.</p>\n<p>Capital: Pratishthana (Paithan).</p>\n<p>Greatest Ruler: Gautamiputra Satakarni.</p>\n<p>Religion: Buddhism.</p>\n<p>Significance: Patronized Buddhism. Land grants to Brahmins started.</p>\n<p>Trade: With Rome. Roman coins found in South India.</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Sangam Age (300 BC - 300 AD)</h3>\n<p>Region: Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka.</p>\n<p>Three Kingdoms: Chera (Kerala), Chola (Tamil Nadu), Pandya (Madurai).</p>\n<p>Sangam Literature: Tolkappiyam (Tamil grammar), Silappadikaram, Manimekalai.</p>\n<p>Trade: With Rome. Roman coins found in South India.</p>\n<p>Society: Matriarchal in some areas.</p>\n<p>Religion: Buddhism, Jainism, and Hinduism.</p>\n<h3>Part 6: Foreign Invasions</h3>\n<p>Indo-Greeks | 2nd Century BC | North-West India</p>\n<p>Shakas | 1st Century BC | North-West India</p>\n<p>Parthians | 1st Century AD | North-West India</p>\n<p>Kushanas | 1st Century AD | North-West India</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Important Facts for SSC</h3>\n<p>Founder of Shunga Dynasty | Pushyamitra Shunga</p>\n<p>Shunga Capital | Pataliputra</p>\n<p>Shunga Religion | Brahmanism</p>\n<p>Patanjali | Wrote Mahabhashya</p>\n<p>Founder of Kushana Dynasty | Kujula Kadphises</p>\n<p>Greatest Kushana Ruler | Kanishka</p>\n<p>Kushana Capital | Purushapura (Peshawar)</p>\n<p>Kanishka's Religion | Buddhism</p>\n<p>4th Buddhist Council | Kundalvana (Kashmir)</p>\n<p>Kanishka's Court Poets | Ashvaghosha, Vasumitra</p>\n<p>Founder of Satavahana Dynasty | Simuka</p>\n<p>Greatest Satavahana Ruler | Gautamiputra Satakarni</p>\n<p>Satavahana Capital | Pratishthana (Paithan)</p>\n<p>Land Grants | Started by Satavahanas</p>\n<p>Sangam Age | Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka</p>\n<p>Three Kingdoms | Chera, Chola, Pandya</p>\n<p>Sangam Literature | Tolkappiyam, Silappadikaram, Manimekalai</p>\n<p>Trade | With Rome</p>\n<p>Roman Coins | Found in South India</p>\n<p><b>Q1: Who founded the Shunga Dynasty? Answer: Pushyamitra Shunga</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2: Who wrote the Mahabhashya? Answer: Patanjali</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3: Who was the greatest Kushana ruler? Answer: Kanishka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4: Where was the 4th Buddhist Council held? Answer: Kundalvana (Kashmir)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5: Who organized the 4th Buddhist Council? Answer: Kanishka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6: Who was the founder of the Satavahana Dynasty? Answer: Simuka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7: Who was the greatest Satavahana ruler? Answer: Gautamiputra Satakarni</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8: What was the capital of the Satavahanas? Answer: Pratishthana (Paithan)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9: What is the famous Tamil grammar book? Answer: Tolkappiyam</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10: Who were the three kingdoms of the Sangam Age? Answer: Chera, Chola, Pandya</b></p>"
