    "body": "<h3>Part 1: What Was the Vijayanagara Empire? ★</h3>\n<h4>🎯 Why Important?</h4>\n<h3>Part 2: Founders — One by One ★</h3>\n<div class='keybox'><b>💡 Simple Explanation:</b></div>\n<h4>🎯 Why Important?</h4>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 13</p>\n<p>Greatest ruler of Vijayanagara Empire. Tuluva Dynasty. Title: Andhra Bhoja. Court poets: Ashtadiggajas. Famous poet: Tenali</p>\n<p>Rama. Wrote Amuktamalyada.</p>\n<p>Feature Detail</p>\n<p>Greatest Ruler Krishnadevaraya</p>\n<p>Dynasty Tuluva Dynasty</p>\n<p>Title Andhra Bhoja</p>\n<p>Court Poets Ashtadiggajas (8 poets)</p>\n<p>Famous Poet Tenali Rama</p>\n<p>Book Amuktamalyada</p>\n<p>Death 1529</p>\n<p>Greatest ruler of Vijayanagara Empire</p>\n<p>Belonged to Tuluva Dynasty</p>\n<p>Title: Andhra Bhoja</p>\n<p>Had eight poets (Ashtadiggajas) in court</p>\n<p>Most famous: Tenali Rama</p>\n<p>Wrote Amuktamalyada</p>\n<p>Died in 1529</p>\n<p>Great warrior and patron of art</p>\n<p>Expanded Vijayanagara Empire</p>\n<h3>Part 3: Krishnadevaraya (1509 – 1529) ★</h3>\n<div class='keybox'><b>💡 Simple Explanation:</b></div>\n<h4>🎯 Why Important?</h4>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 14</p>\n<p>Fought in 1565. Deccan Sultanates joined against Vijayanagara. Vijayanagara defeated. Fatal blow — slow decline followed.</p>\n<p>Feature Detail</p>\n<p>Year 1565</p>\n<p>Place Talikota</p>\n<p>Alliance Against Deccan Sultanates</p>\n<p>Result Vijayanagara defeated</p>\n<p>Significance Fatal blow. Slow decline.</p>\n<p>Fought in 1565</p>\n<p>Deccan Sultanates joined against Vijayanagara</p>\n<p>Vijayanagara defeated</p>\n<p>Fatal blow — not immediate end</p>\n<p>Slow decline followed</p>\n<p>Empire finally ended in 1646</p>\n<p>Fatal blow to Vijayanagara</p>\n<p>Changed political situation in South India</p>\n<p>Slow decline followed</p>\n<h3>Part 4: Battle of Talikota (1565) ★</h3>\n<div class='keybox'><b>💡 Simple Explanation:</b></div>\n<h4>🎯 Why Important?</h4>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 15</p>\n<p>Fact Detail</p>\n<p>Founders Harihara and Bukka</p>\n<p>Year 1336</p>\n<p>Capital Hampi (Vijayanagara)</p>\n<p>Dynasty Sangama Dynasty</p>\n<p>Feudatories Of Kakatiya Dynasty</p>\n<p>Greatest Ruler Krishnadevaraya</p>\n<p>Krishnadevaraya's Dynasty Tuluva Dynasty</p>\n<p>Krishnadevaraya's Title Andhra Bhoja</p>\n<p>Court Poets Ashtadiggajas</p>\n<p>Famous Poet Tenali Rama</p>\n<p>Krishnadevaraya's Book Amuktamalyada</p>\n<p>Battle of Talikota 1565</p>\n<p>Result Vijayanagara defeated</p>\n<p>Significance Fatal blow. Slow decline.</p>\n<p>Empire Ended 1646</p>\n<h3>Part 5: Important Facts for SSC — Quick Revision ★</h3>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 16</p>\n<p><b>Q1. Who founded the Vijayanagara Empire?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Harihara and Bukka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q2. When was the Vijayanagara Empire founded?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: 1336</b></p>\n<p><b>Q3. What was the capital of the Vijayanagara Empire?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Hampi (Vijayanagara)</b></p>\n<p><b>Q4. Who were the feudatories of the Kakatiya Dynasty?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Harihara and Bukka</b></p>\n<p><b>Q5. Who was the greatest ruler of the Vijayanagara Empire?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Krishnadevaraya</b></p>\n<p><b>Q6. What was Krishnadevaraya's title?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Andhra Bhoja</b></p>\n<p><b>Q7. Who were the Ashtadiggajas?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: 8 poets in Krishnadevaraya's court</b></p>\n<p><b>Q8. Who was the most famous poet in Krishnadevaraya's court?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Tenali Rama</b></p>\n<p><b>Q9. Which book did Krishnadevaraya write?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Amuktamalyada</b></p>\n<p><b>Q10. When was the Battle of Talikota fought?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: 1565</b></p>\n<p><b>Q11. What was the result of the Battle of Talikota?</b></p>\n<p><b>Answer: Vijayanagara defeated. Fatal blow. Slow decline.</b></p>\n<h3>Part 6: Previous Year Questions — Q1 to Q11 ★</h3>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 17</p>\n<p>👑 Founders</p>\n<p>Harihara and Bukka (1336)</p>\n<p>Feudatories of Kakatiya Dynasty</p>\n<p>Capital: Hampi (Vijayanagara)</p>\n<p>Dynasty: Sangama Dynasty</p>\n<p>👑 Krishnadevaraya (1509-1529)</p>\n<p>Greatest ruler</p>\n<p>Dynasty: Tuluva Dynasty</p>\n<p>Title: Andhra Bhoja</p>\n<p>Court Poets: Ashtadiggajas</p>\n<p>Famous Poet: Tenali Rama</p>\n<p>Book: Amuktamalyada</p>\n<p>⚔️ Battle of Talikota (1565)</p>\n<p>Alliance: Deccan Sultanates</p>\n<p>Result: Vijayanagara defeated</p>\n<p>Significance: Fatal blow. Slow decline.</p>\n<p>Empire finally ended: 1646</p>\n<h3>Part 7: Summary — Vijayanagara Empire ★</h3>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 18</p>\n<p>🎯 Remember</p>\n<p>Harihara and Bukka: Founders (1336)</p>\n<p>Hampi: Capital</p>\n<p>Krishnadevaraya: Greatest ruler. Andhra Bhoja.</p>\n<p>Tenali Rama: Famous poet</p>\n<p>Amuktamalyada: Book by Krishnadevaraya</p>\n<p>Battle of Talikota: 1565. Fatal blow.</p>\n<h3>Part 7 (Continued): Remember + Final Tip ★</h3>\n<p>🎓 Final Tip: Remember the founders (Harihara and Bukka, 1336), the greatest ruler</p>\n<p>(Krishnadevaraya), his title (Andhra Bhoja), the famous poet (Tenali Rama), and the Battle of</p>\n<p>Talikota (1565). These are the most asked facts in SSC exams!</p>\n<p>📌</p>\n<p>Vijayanagara Empire — Complete Guide Page 19</p>\n<p>Bhakti Movement: Religious reform movement in Hinduism. Emphasized devotion to God. Rejected rituals and caste system.</p>\n<p>Sufi Movement: Religious reform movement in Islam. Emphasized love and devotion to God. Rejected rituals and orthodoxy.</p>\n<p>Bhakti Movement: 7th–17th Century AD</p>\n<p>Sufi Movement: 10th–17th Century AD</p>\n<p>Promoted love, equality, devotion</p>\n<p>Rejected rituals and caste system</p>\n<p>Brought Hindus and Muslims closer</p>\n<p>Great saint. Born 1440 in Varanasi. Promoted Hindu-Muslim unity. Followers: Kabir Panth. Wrote dohe in Hindi.</p>\n<p>Feature Detail</p>\n<p>Born 1440, Varanasi</p>\n<p>Religion Hindu-Muslim unity</p>\n<p>Followers Kabir Panth</p>\n<p>Language Hindi</p>\n<p>Famous Dohe &quot;Kaal Kare So Aaj Kar&quot;</p>\n<p>Significance Promoted Hindu-Muslim unity</p>\n<p>Born in 1440 in Varanasi</p>\n<p>Promoted Hindu-Muslim unity</p>\n<p>Rejected rituals and caste system</p>\n<p>Followers: Kabir Panth</p>\n<p>Wrote dohe (couplets) in Hindi</p>\n<p>🕉️🕉️ BBhhaakkt</p>\n<p>ti</p>\n<p>i aanndd SSuuf</p>\n<p>fi</p>\n<p>i MMoovveemmeennt</p>\n<p>tss</p>\n<p>MEDIEVAL INDIA — CHAPTER 5</p>\n<p>Complete Notes with Explanation</p>"
